@startuml seq-replay-golden
title Golden-record system test and parallel rollouts [PROPOSED]

== golden test (one per script, ctest label golden) ==
participant "trc_golden_test" as Test
participant "compareWithGolden\n(hexrecord)" as Cmp
participant Session
participant ScriptedPlayer
participant "writeRecord\n(canonical)" as Writer

Test -> Cmp : compareWithGolden(slug.script.xml, slug.golden.xml, definition, policies, grammar)
Cmp -> Session : sessionFor(record) (scenario position, seed)
loop each move in the script
  Cmp -> ScriptedPlayer : choose(session, side)
  ScriptedPlayer --> Cmp : Command
  Cmp -> Session : apply(Command)
  Session --> Cmp : Applied (events, draws)
end
Cmp -> Writer : writeRecord(slug.actual.xml, Golden, session, log)
Cmp -> Cmp : byte compare with slug.golden.xml ; first divergent move if not equal
Cmp --> Test : GoldenReport{matchP, first, unifiedDiff, actualWritten}
note over Test
  On mismatch the report prints the move, golden vs
  actual outcome and draw, the diff, and the re-bless
  command. Goldens are never edited by hand.
end note

== parallel rollouts (parallel_rollout_test, hexgames_bench) ==
participant Main
participant "Session (root)" as Root
collections "Session (fork) x N" as Forks
Main -> Root : Session(definition, policies, position, seed)
Main -> Root : fork() x N (Position, streams, scratch copied; definition shared const)
Main -> Forks : each on its own std::thread: play(RandomPlayer on Player streams, 200 commands)
Forks --> Main : final digests
Main -> Main : each equals its serial twin; no data race under the sanitizers
@enduml
